{"name":"Satsuma Imo Red","hex":"#96466a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"satsuma","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A seedless and easy-peeling cultivar of mandarin orange of Japanese origin; Citrus unshiu."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satsuma"},{"term":"imo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Imbongu."]},{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["Alternative form of IMO."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imo"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet potato","blocks":[{"text":"The sweet potato or sweetpotato is a dicotyledonous plant in the morning glory family, Convolvulaceae. Its sizeable, starchy, sweet-tasting, tuberous roots are used as a root vegetable, which is a staple food in parts of the world. Cultivars of the sweet potato have been bred to bear tubers with flesh and skin of various colors. Moreover, the young shoots and leaves are eaten as greens with nutritional composition comparable to spinach. The sweet potato and the potato are only distantly related, both being in the order Solanales. Although darker sweet potatoes are often known as yams in parts of North America, they are even more distant from actual yams, which are monocots in the order Dioscoreales."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Ipomoea_batatas_006.JPG/330px-Ipomoea_batatas_006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_potato"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Genasu_gadde_%28Kannada_%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%86%E0%B2%A3%E0%B2%B8%E0%B3%81_%E0%B2%97%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%8D%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%86%29_%2849108875711%29.jpg/500px-Genasu_gadde_%28Kannada_%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%86%E0%B2%A3%E0%B2%B8%E0%B3%81_%E0%B2%97%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%8D%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%86%29_%2849108875711%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Genasu_gadde_%28Kannada_%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%86%E0%B2%A3%E0%B2%B8%E0%B3%81_%E0%B2%97%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%8D%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%86%29_%2849108875711%29.jpg/1280px-Genasu_gadde_%28Kannada_%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%86%E0%B2%A3%E0%B2%B8%E0%B3%81_%E0%B2%97%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%8D%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%86%29_%2849108875711%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Genasu_gadde_%28Kannada_%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%86%E0%B2%A3%E0%B2%B8%E0%B3%81_%E0%B2%97%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%8D%E0%B2%A1%E0%B3%86%29_%2849108875711%29.jpg/500px-Genasu_gadde_%28Kannada_%E0%B2%97%E0%B3%86%E0%B2%A3%E0%B2%B8%E